## Architecture

This app is built on the [platform-infra](https://github.com/{{ github_handle }}/platform-infra) stack.

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | FastAPI (Python 3.12), served via DigitalOcean App Platform |
| Database | PostgreSQL on a shared managed cluster (private VPC) |
| Cache / Queue | Redis on a shared managed instance |
{% if include_frontend %}
| Frontend | Next.js (TypeScript), deployed to DigitalOcean App Platform |
{% endif %}
{% if include_ios %}
| iOS | SwiftUI |
{% endif %}
| Infrastructure | Pulumi (Python), stack `{{ pulumi_org }}/{{ app_name }}/prod` |
| Auth | Clerk |
| Feature Flags | Flagsmith |
| Error Tracking | Sentry |
| Observability | Honeycomb |

## Local Development

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+, [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
{% if include_frontend %}
- Node.js 20+
{% endif %}
- Docker (for local Postgres + Redis)

### Backend

```bash
# Copy and fill in environment variables (pydantic-settings reads from backend/.env)
cp .env.example backend/.env

# Start local Postgres + Redis
docker compose up -d

# Install dependencies and run
cd backend
uv sync
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

The API will be available at http://localhost:8000.
{% if include_frontend %}

### Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

The frontend will be available at http://localhost:3000.
{% endif %}

## Tests

```bash
cd backend
uv run pytest
```

## Environment Variables

See `.env.example` for all required variables and documentation. In production,
these are injected by Pulumi as App Platform secrets — you never manage them manually.

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | PostgreSQL connection string (asyncpg driver) |
| `REDIS_URL` | Redis connection URL |
| `DEBUG` | Enable debug mode (default: `false`) |
| `ENVIRONMENT` | Runtime environment (`development` / `production`) |
{% if include_frontend %}
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | Backend API URL for the frontend |
{% endif %}
| `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` | Clerk authentication secret |
| `FLAGSMITH_API_KEY` | Flagsmith environment API key |
| `SENTRY_DSN` | Sentry DSN for error reporting |
| `HONEYCOMB_API_KEY` | Honeycomb API key for observability |

## Deployment

Merge to `main` — GitHub Actions handles everything:

1. `pulumi up` provisions/updates all infrastructure
2. DigitalOcean App Platform redeploys from the latest commit automatically

No manual deploy steps are needed.

## Post-Scaffold Setup

After scaffolding this repo for the first time:

**1. Create per-app SaaS resources:**

```bash
# Set your admin tokens in the environment first
export FLAGSMITH_SERVER_API_KEY=...
export SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=...
export SENTRY_ORG=...
export HONEYCOMB_API_KEY=...

bash scripts/setup-saas.sh
```

**2. Store the resulting keys as Pulumi config secrets** (this is what injects them into the app at runtime via App Platform):

```bash
cd infra
pulumi config set --secret clerk_secret_key  "sk_live_..."
pulumi config set --secret flagsmith_api_key "..."
pulumi config set --secret sentry_dsn        "https://...@sentry.io/..."
pulumi config set --secret honeycomb_api_key "..."
```

**3. Add CI credentials as GitHub Actions secrets** (these are only needed by the deploy workflow, not by the app itself):

```bash
gh secret set PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN --body "..."
gh secret set DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN  --body "..."
```

**4. Deploy infrastructure:**

```bash
cd infra
pulumi stack init prod   # first time only — creates the stack in Pulumi Cloud
pulumi up
```

## GitHub Actions Secrets Required

| Secret | Description |
|---|---|
| `PULUMI_ACCESS_TOKEN` | Pulumi Cloud token (used by deploy workflow) |
| `DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN` | DigitalOcean API token (used by deploy workflow) |

SaaS credentials (`CLERK_SECRET_KEY`, `FLAGSMITH_API_KEY`, `SENTRY_DSN`,
`HONEYCOMB_API_KEY`) are stored as **Pulumi config secrets**, not GitHub secrets.
Pulumi injects them directly into App Platform as runtime environment variables.

## Feature Flags

Feature flags are managed in [Flagsmith](https://flagsmith.com). To add a flag:

1. Create the flag in the Flagsmith dashboard for this project
2. Read it in Python:
   ```python
   from flagsmith import Flagsmith
   flagsmith = Flagsmith(environment_key=settings.flagsmith_api_key)
   is_enabled = flagsmith.is_feature_enabled("my-feature")
   ```

